Author: Marius Momeu <marius.momeu@berkeley.edu>
Date:   Sun Nov 15 01:28:26 2026 +0000

    integer.h: port 12 items (wave-223/batch-0/run-1)

    fn::git__is_int
    fn::git__is_sizet
    fn::git__is_ssizet
    fn::git__is_uint16
    fn::git__is_uint32
    fn::git__is_ulong
    mac::git__add_int64_overflow
    mac::git__add_int_overflow
    mac::git__add_sizet_overflow
    mac::git__multiply_int64_overflow
    mac::git__multiply_sizet_overflow
    mac::git__sub_int_overflow

    The six range checks are fits_usize, fits_isize, fits_u16, fits_u32,
    fits_c_ulong and fits_c_int, generic over TryInto, and the six macros the
    const fns checked_{add,mul}_usize, checked_{add,sub}_c_int and
    checked_{add,mul}_i64, over std's checked_*, None on overflow. The module
    is native, with no unsafe region and no export: the header stays for the
    C that includes it. Its docs name the macros' <intsafe.h> and GIT_INLINE
    branches, and the four inputs on which git__multiply_int64_overflow's
    fallback answers otherwise; and the C round trips the ports do not copy:
    git__is_ssizet is always true, and git__is_sizet and git__is_ulong accept
    negative values on this 64-bit build.

    Twelve unit_pub tests carry over tests/util/integer.c's three cases and
    test_errors__integer_overflow_sets_oom's inputs; seven equiv tests compare
    the range checks through six new static_fns.c wrappers (allowlisted for
    the equivalence tests only) and the macros where they expand, in
    git__calloc, git__mallocarray, git__reallocarray,
    git_strlist_copy_with_null and git_config_parse_int64.
    git__add_int_overflow and git__sub_int_overflow expand only in
    patch_parse.c, which no binding reaches. Proposal:
    config-branches-the-target-never-builds (porting-symbols).

    Co-Authored-By: crustify <crustify@berkeley.edu>

